CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T9, "Lineage and rebirth")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T9_SUB, "Lifespan, imprints, perks, the collection")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T9_P1, "Each realm gives a lifespan, and only reading ages you: one reading hour is a year. Past 80% of it the Cultivator screen shows the years left; at the end the life is over and a new one begins. A breakthrough raises the lifespan, so it only bites after a long stall.\nFrom Foundation Establishment you may reincarnate any time from the Lineage cell. A life gives imprints: 2 for Foundation, 4 Core Formation, 7 Nascent Soul and more later, +1 for each Dao found and +1 for every 8 new codex entries. Abandoning a life is allowed any time and gives none.")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T9_P2, "Imprints buy legacy perks when a life ends: more destiny rolls, luck in ruins, a scroll carried over, starting stones, a charted first region, known recipes, your old rival back. Perks last for every life to come.\nThe best realm any life has reached gives every later life +3% Qi for each realm past Foundation Establishment, up to +21%. It never adds up across lives.\nMementos turn up when a region is cleared, in caves, in ruins and now and then from the daily tasks. They and the codex stay with the lineage. Every old Chronicle is kept under Chronicle > Past lives.")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T10, "Days and the clock")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T10_SUB, "What a day is, with or without the date")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T10_P1, "The omen, the daily tasks, the streak, your rival and the ranking go by days. With the date set, a day is a calendar day: read in as many sittings as you like, it is still one day.\nWithout the date (the original X4 has no clock, and a reader whose clock was never set has none either), the game counts reading days instead. A reading day ends when you open the game after the reader has slept, once you have read at least an hour since the last one began. Sittings without a sleep in between are always the same day.\nOn reading days your rival trains one day per reading day, the streak counts reading days in a row, and the weekly allowance does not apply. Set the date and the calendar takes over again; the change counts as one day.")
